    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1599">

                <pb facs="1010" n="894" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg894"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/100.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Chargé d’Affaires
                        to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Imperial German Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Newport</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: A telegraphic report
                    from the Imperial Consulate at Guadalajara, which did not reach Berlin until the
                    end of July, says that when the Constitutionalist forces took that city on the
                    8th of last month they respected the interests of German residents.</p>
                <p>I am instructed to express to the Government of the United States the Imperial
                    Government’s thanks for the friendly readiness with which the threatened German
                    interests were again looked after in this case in a specially effective
                    manner.</p>
                <p>In having the honor thus to comply with the aforesaid instructions, I have
                    reference to your excellency’s obliging note verbale of June 20th last on the
                        subject.<anchor n="153" xml:id="d1599-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Haniel</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1599-f1" n="153" xml:id="d1599-f1-content">
                <p>Communicated to the German Ambassador, June 20, 1914.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
